A dead letter is a sync operation that failed and **cannot be retried** — a bad signature, a hash mismatch, an unrecoverable transport error. It is the terminal category, distinct from the transient failures that the channel retries with exponential backoff.

When a channel routes an operation to its dead-letter mailbox the sync manager does four things: logs it, quarantines the document, persists a record to dead-letter storage, and emits `DEAD_LETTER_ADDED` (20004).

```typescript
type DeadLetterAddedEvent = {
  id: string;
  jobId: string;
  remoteName: string;
  documentId: string;
  errorSource: ChannelErrorSource; // none | channel | inbox | outbox
};
```

The design decision worth internalizing is the **granularity of the quarantine: per document, not per drive.** Once a document is quarantined, its inbound operations are dropped and its outbound operations are filtered out of the outbox — but every other document on the same remote keeps syncing normally. A single corrupt or unverifiable document therefore degrades to a hole in the replica rather than a stalled drive. Without this, one bad operation would head-of-line block an entire collection.

The flip side is that quarantine is silent unless you watch for it. Nothing retries automatically and nothing surfaces in the drive's own status, so `DEAD_LETTER_ADDED` is the event to subscribe to for anything that needs manual intervention. The `errorSource` tag tells you which stage produced it (`inbox`, `outbox`, or the `channel` itself), which is usually enough to separate "the remote sent us something bad" from "we produced something the remote rejected".

Retention is bounded: each remote keeps at most `maxDeadLettersPerRemote` dead letters, default `100`, configurable via `SyncBuilder.withMaxDeadLettersPerRemote(limit)`. Past that the oldest are evicted — so dead-letter storage is a recent-failures buffer for diagnostics, not a durable audit log. If you need the full record, capture the events as they fire.

_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/04-Synchronization.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._
